{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EnHnr8yrFUZq5c4eehdYd2","type":"tool_result","content":"NOTES.md\nREADME.md\nbot.py\ndata/athletes.json\nlogs/usage.jsonl\n# Notes\n\n## 2026-04-20 — bill doubled since memory shipped\n\nInput spend roughly doubled in the week after `save_fact` went live (2026-04-13),\nwith the same number of messages per day. `logs/usage.jsonl` shows it: on a normal\nmessage the loop rounds and the next message read ~1000 tokens from cache, but\nevery call right after a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1000 again. Athletes tell the bot things about\nthemselves a lot in their first week, so this happens several times per chat.\n\nTried: shorter facts (no change), capping facts at 20 (no change, the number of\nfacts is not the problem). Tool filtering by keyword is from March and was a clear\nwin (~75% fewer tool tokens on short messages); leave it.\n# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:09+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 2, \"input_tokens\": 133, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 1334, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 161}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:26+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 23, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1090, \"output_tokens\": 79}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:56+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 61, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1090, \"output_tokens\": 41, \"tool\": \"save_fact\"}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:05:39+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 2, \"input_tokens\": 139, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 1104, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 155}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:05:54+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 26, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1104, \"output_tokens\": 93}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"899187cc-1edb-4442-86f2-7a3dc7ad3aa5","uuid":"2b522b07-e97c-473e-bbe1-9d39c5b801c6","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:05:05.024Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"NOTES.md\nREADME.md\nbot.py\ndata/athletes.json\nlogs/usage.jsonl\n# Notes\n\n## 2026-04-20 — bill doubled since memory shipped\n\nInput spend roughly doubled in the week after `save_fact` went live (2026-04-13),\nwith the same number of messages per day. `logs/usage.jsonl` shows it: on a normal\nmessage the loop rounds and the next message read ~1000 tokens from cache, but\nevery call right after a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and\n`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1000 again. Athletes tell the bot things about\nthemselves a lot in their first week, so this happens several times per chat.\n\nTried: shorter facts (no change), capping facts at 20 (no change, the number of\nfacts is not the problem). Tool filtering by keyword is from March and was a clear\nwin (~75% fewer tool tokens on short messages); leave it.\n# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:09+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 2, \"input_tokens\": 133, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 1334, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 161}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:26+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 23, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1090, \"output_tokens\": 79}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:04:56+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 61, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1090, \"output_tokens\": 41, \"tool\": \"save_fact\"}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:05:39+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 2, \"input_tokens\": 139, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 1104, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 155}\n{\"ts\": \"2026-04-18T08:05:54+00:00\", \"user\": \"42\", \"round\": 1, \"input_tokens\": 26, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 1104, \"output_tokens\": 93}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EnHnr8yrFUZq5c4eehdYd2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
